{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And she was hidden and she became impure.</b> From here: a case of doubtful impurity in a private domain — its doubt is impure. For every 'hiding' is only in a private domain, and we see here that the Merciful One forbade on the basis of doubt." "<b>And she became impure.</b> By the semen of the one who lay with her. <b>והיא נטמאה</b> is written with a yud." "<b>And there is no witness against her.</b> That she became impure — and why 'there is no witness against her'? Because she was not caught, and since she is in doubt she requires investigation." "<b>And there is no witness against her.</b> What Rashi explained — 'the implication is that if there is a witness against her' etc. — that he explained. But it is like 'ורגמו אותו' (Deut. 22:24) without its suffix — the implication is 'אותה' with its suffix etc. — 'the chapter of those executed by court'; and so in the Mekhilta. And even though he wrote in the Rashi commentary that it is a scribal error, and so we learned in Sotah: Tanna of the school of Rabbi Yishmael — why did the Torah trust a single witness in the case of a sotah? It is a foothold for the matter, for he had been jealous of her, as it is written, ועבר עליו רוח קנאה — that he was jealous, that is, he had warned her, and she went and was hidden, and a single witness testifies that she became impure. And so we learned in tractate Ketubot: a woman is not forbidden to her husband on the testimony of one witness, but with two witnesses; but warning and seclusion — even with one witness. And what Rashi explained, that 'there is no witness against her' refers to impurity but there are witnesses to the seclusion — he goes back and explains, and that is what we learned in Sotah: 'ועד אין בה' — בה, and not in the warning; בה, and not in the seclusion. And Rashi: בה refers to impurity, for it follows from what came before it — והיא נטמאה ועד אין בה — and we derive: there are not two witnesses against her but one; בה, a single witness is trusted, and not for the warning and not for the seclusion." "<b>And she was not caught.</b> At the time of the act of intercourse."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {3 "The phrase 'ובמ״א' (u-vi-Mekhilta, 'and so in the Mekhilta') appears corrupted in this witness; the reading is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:39.603163019Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}